    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0095" n="7" sameAs="frus:frus1933v04/pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.G 1A/147: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-07-17T16:00:00-05:00">July 17, 1933—4
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:44 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>65. Legation’s 62, July 13, 8 p.m. Olaya<anchor n="12" xml:id="d10-f1"/> says
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs misunderstood his idea. What he hopes for is
                    presentation by the United States at Seventh Pan-American Conference of
                    resolution or other document embodying all proposals in President Roosevelt’s
                    disarmament message.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d10-f1" n="12" xml:id="d10-f1-content">
                <p>Enrique Olaya-Herrera, President of Colombia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
